+---
+id: task-005-add-createpatch-rfc-6902-diff
+type: task
+title: "Add createPatch (RFC 6902 diff)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two JSON documents. Export `createPatch(from, to)` from
+`src/index.ts`: it returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from` into `to` under `applyPatch`, without
+mutating either input. The patch describes only what changed: objects are diffed member by member; arrays by
+longest common subsequence, so an inserted or removed item is a single `add`/`remove` and a moved item a
+`remove` plus an `add`, never a rewrite of neighbours. Done: implemented, round-trip, minimality, move,
+no-mutation/aliasing and `__proto__` tests pass, README documents it.
